    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22300" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incensor</span></b> , ōris, m.
		incendo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>one who kindles</i> or <i>sets fire
			to</i> (post-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">messium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig. 48, 19, 16, § 9</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Paul. Sent. 5, 20</span></i>; Mos. et
			Rom. Leg. Coll. 12, 3, 2: specularum, i. e. <i>who
				kindles beacons</i>, App. de Mundo, p. 69. —
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>an inciter</i>, <i>instigator</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">turbarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 31, 9, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
